From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ville Takio <ville+git@takio.fi>
Subject: [PATCH] b43: AC-PHY: allow 40 MHz on 2.4 GHz

With the farrow resampler and the bandwidth-scaled registers programmed
as wl 7.14 does on 2.4 GHz, 40 MHz works there: on the RT-AC66U B1 at
ch6/40 a 1x1 client gets 60 Mbit/s up and 91 Mbit/s down (7 Mbit/s down
before). Stop masking HT40 on the 2.4 GHz band.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -7013,14 +7013,9 @@ static int b43_setup_bands(struct b43_wl
 	if (dev->phy.type == B43_PHYTYPE_AC && have_2ghz_phy) {
 		struct ieee80211_supported_band *band = &dev->wl->band_2ghz_ac;
 
-		/*
-		 * HT on 2.4 GHz as on 5 GHz, at 20 MHz only: 40 MHz on 2.4 GHz
-		 * has no capture (docs/retrace-todo.md, "2.4 GHz"). No VHT.
-		 */
+		/* HT on 2.4 GHz as on 5 GHz, at 20 and 40 MHz. No VHT. */
 		*band = b43_band_2GHz;
 		b43_ac_set_ht_vht_cap(dev, band);
-		band->ht_cap.cap &= ~(IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SUP_WIDTH_20_40 |
-				      IEEE80211_HT_CAP_SGI_40);
 		memset(&band->vht_cap, 0, sizeof(band->vht_cap));
 		hw->wiphy->bands[NL80211_BAND_2GHZ] = band;
 	}
